eator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Poulomi Ghosh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135544012,imgsize-122014.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Texas court reopens Houston home ownership dispute after foreclosure and reverse mortgage]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135540610.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A Texas appeals court has reopened a lengthy dispute over home ownership in Houston, which has complicated legal issues. The case involves multiple foreclosures, reverse mortgages, and unclear ownership claims spanning twenty-five years. Key questions remain about the validity of a 2011 mortgage after a previous foreclosure occurred in 2001. This ruling requires lower courts to thoroughly examine competing ownership claims before making decisions.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-houston-couple-lost-their-home-in-a-2001-foreclosure-yet-signed-a-reverse-mortgage-in-2011-after-an-hoa-foreclosure-and-a-new-buyer-a-texas-appeals-court-reopened-the-fight-over-who-had-a-valid-claim/articleshow/135540610.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-houston-couple-lost-their-home-in-a-2001-foreclosure-yet-signed-a-reverse-mortgage-in-2011-after-an-hoa-foreclosure-and-a-new-buyer-a-texas-appeals-court-reopened-the-fight-over-who-had-a-valid-claim/articleshow/135540610.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-04T20:29:14+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135543237,imgsize-214635.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Texas parents honor daughter’s rescuers through a foundation that has awarded 67 scholarships]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135543272.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Tragedy struck when 18-year-old student Kenli Riney died in a highway accident in Texas, with the Argote family making valiant attempts to save her. To commemorate her spirit, they founded the Kenli Foundation, which offers scholarships to young individuals showing courage and kindness. Additionally, they introduced the Argote Award Scholarship to recognize and reward the remarkable bravery of those who come to the aid of others.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2021-a-texas-teen-died-after-strangers-tried-to-pull-her-from-a-burning-car-her-parents-turned-the-rescuers-courage-into-a-scholarship-foundation-that-has-since-given-67000-to-67-recipients/articleshow/135543272.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2021-a-texas-teen-died-after-strangers-tried-to-pull-her-from-a-burning-car-her-parents-turned-the-rescuers-courage-into-a-scholarship-foundation-that-has-since-given-67000-to-67-recipients/articleshow/135543272.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-04T20:40:28+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135543586,imgsize-80388.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Zac Brown's 11.5-acre farm feeds campers at Georgia charity supporting children and veterans]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135543326.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Founded by Zac Brown in 2011, Camp Southern Ground is a beacon of inclusivity for children and veterans. Spanning 400 acres, its campus includes an organic farm that not only provides nutritious meals but also offers educational initiatives. Over the years, Camp Southern Ground has evolved to enhance support for military families, using a rounded approach that fosters personal growth through food, outdoor activities, and community engagement.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/zac-brown-founded-camp-southern-ground-in-georgia-in-2011-15-years-later-its-11-5-acre-organic-farm-helps-feed-campers-while-programmes-support-children-veterans-and-military-families/articleshow/135543326.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/zac-brown-founded-camp-southern-ground-in-georgia-in-2011-15-years-later-its-11-5-acre-organic-farm-helps-feed-campers-while-programmes-support-children-veterans-and-military-families/articleshow/135543326.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-04T20:57:11+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135543515,imgsize-85260.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Spokane judge bars two children from inheriting $600M estate over exploitation finding]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135538862.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/spokane-real-estate-magnate-harlan-douglass-left-an-estate-of-about-600-million-on-october-26-a-judge-ruled-two-of-his-three-children-financially-exploited-him-as-he-lived-with-dementia-barring-them-from-inheriting/articleshow/135538862.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/spokane-real-estate-magnate-harlan-douglass-left-an-estate-of-about-600-million-on-october-26-a-judge-ruled-two-of-his-three-children-financially-exploited-him-as-he-lived-with-dementia-barring-them-from-inheriting/articleshow/135538862.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-04T20:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135538987,imgsize-645479.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Ed Sheeran gets approval to restore six historic barns for private music archive and studios]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135541252.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Ed Sheeran has secured permission to renovate six barns on his Suffolk estate, intending to create a private music archive while preserving the barns' 19th-century charm. This thoughtful restoration seeks to minimize major changes to the structures, ensuring that the project also promotes local wildlife and biodiversity, showcasing Sheeran's dedication to his music, heritage, and the surrounding environment.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/ed-sheeran-received-approval-in-october-2026-to-restore-six-deteriorating-barns-on-a-historic-suffolk-farm-for-his-private-music-archive-alongside-previously-approved-plans-to-turn-an-old-piggery-into-studios/articleshow/135541252.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/ed-sheeran-received-approval-in-october-2026-to-restore-six-deteriorating-barns-on-a-historic-suffolk-farm-for-his-private-music-archive-alongside-previously-approved-plans-to-turn-an-old-piggery-into-studios/articleshow/135541252.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-04T20:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135541449,imgsize-96066.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[From Iran to India: How Trump's midterm loss could affect America's foreign policy]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135541084.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/from-iran-to-india-how-trumps-midterm-loss-could-affect-americas-foreign-policy/articleshow/135541084.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/from-iran-to-india-how-trumps-midterm-loss-could-affect-americas-foreign-policy/articleshow/135541084.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-04T19:27:19+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Prisha Patnaik</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135541260,imgsize-263420.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[H-1B, immigration and Trump: Why Indian-American voters turned away from Republicans]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135540281.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[With Democrats gaining Congressional control, Indian-Americans are grappling with uncertainty regarding immigration rules and job opportunities. Heightened fears about H-1B visa restrictions and deportation have taken center stage. In addition, increasing discrimination and the prevailing political climate are altering feelings of identity among the community. New survey data reveals a trend towards favoring Democratic candidates, indicating that the outcomes of the midterms might significantly influence the Indian-American experience.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/us-mid-term-elections/news/h-1b-immigration-and-trump-why-indian-american-voters-are-reconsidering-republicans/articleshow/135540281.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/us-mid-term-elections/news/h-1b-immigration-and-trump-why-indian-american-voters-are-reconsidering-republicans/articleshow/135540281.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-04T19:22:03+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Trisha Mahajan</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135541980,imgsize-81412.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Man who inherited £50m Cornwall estate after DNA test found guilty in pub fight]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135540080.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Jordan Adlard-Rogers recently discovered he is the rightful heir to the Penrose Estate after a DNA test confirmed his lineage. However, his newfound status is marred by legal issues stemming from a wedding altercation where he punched another guest, causing severe injuries that required surgery. Although he claimed self-defense, a jury dismissed his argument, leaving his future uncertain as he awaits sentencing on December 11.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/jordan-adlard-rogers-inherited-a-50m-cornwall-estate-after-a-dna-test-a-uk-jury-has-now-found-him-guilty-of-grievous-bodily-harm-in-a-2024-pub-fight/articleshow/135540080.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/jordan-adlard-rogers-inherited-a-50m-cornwall-estate-after-a-dna-test-a-uk-jury-has-now-found-him-guilty-of-grievous-bodily-harm-in-a-2024-pub-fight/articleshow/135540080.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-04T19:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135540290,imgsize-77410.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Georgia court revives tenants' claims after mistaken 2022 apartment raid and detention]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135540272.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[The Georgia Court of Appeals has delivered a significant ruling regarding tenant safety rights in a case involving an off-duty police officer and residents of Roswell Creek Apartments. The court has reinstated accusations of assault and false imprisonment against the property owner, stemming from the officer's actions. This landmark decision may pave the way for heightened accountability in property management concerning tenant security.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2022-georgia-police-entered-a-rented-apartment-thinking-it-was-vacant-and-detained-two-men-four-years-later-an-appeals-court-revived-parts-of-their-case-against-the-complex-that-employed-an-officer/articleshow/135540272.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2022-georgia-police-entered-a-rented-apartment-thinking-it-was-vacant-and-detained-two-men-four-years-later-an-appeals-court-revived-parts-of-their-case-against-the-complex-that-employed-an-officer/articleshow/135540272.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-04T18:45:56+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135540449,imgsize-125343.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[French blood plasma storage hit by hackers in widening cyberattack campaign]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135540237.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/french-blood-plasma-storage-hit-by-hackers-in-widening-cyberattack-campaign/articleshow/135540237.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/french-blood-plasma-storage-hit-by-hackers-in-widening-cyberattack-campaign/articleshow/135540237.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-04T18:47:19+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Prisha Patnaik</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135540480,imgsize-126954.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Oregon couple turn lawn into garden, deliver 10 tons of free food]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135540372.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/an-oregon-couple-turned-part-of-their-one-acre-lawn-into-a-vegetable-garden-it-has-now-helped-deliver-10-tons-of-free-food-to-families-in-need/articleshow/135540372.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/an-oregon-couple-turned-part-of-their-one-acre-lawn-into-a-vegetable-garden-it-has-now-helped-deliver-10-tons-of-free-food-to-families-in-need/articleshow/135540372.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-04T18:55:22+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135540660,imgsize-2189002.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Paris Jackson asks court to move $600 million into Michael Jackson's trust 17 years after his death]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135536975.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In a legal move, Paris Jackson has petitioned the court for a $600 million transfer to the family trust. While the estate has generated significant income since Michael Jackson's passing, his children have yet to see the trust funded. Its executors cite unresolved tax matters as a barrier. Paris believes that as she and her brothers near their thirties, distributions should begin.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2009-michael-jackson-left-a-trust-for-his-three-children-17-years-later-daughter-paris-is-asking-a-court-to-move-600-million-into-it-while-estate-executors-say-unresolved-tax-litigation-prevents-full-funding/articleshow/135536975.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.